      "source": "https://www.eup-planning.org/communities/luce-county/mcmillan-township/village-of-newberry/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village houses the Tahquamenon Logging Museum, which tells the story of the area's timber industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.eup-planning.org/communities/luce-county/mcmillan-township/village-of-newberry/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Newberry is the county seat of Luce County, becoming so when the county split from Chippewa in 1887.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newberry%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic Luce County Historical Museum occupies the former sheriff's house, preserved after a 1970s courthouse fight.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newberry%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Newberry sits at the southern gateway to Tahquamenon Falls, surrounded by state and national forests.",
